& [CanonicalRecord: PostFSC5ImplementationReadiness] is the processed planning authority for the post-FSC5 implementation readiness surface
  + [canonical_uuid] is df137ce3-6355-45d2-bec3-e0fadb97dab4
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is 01566e74-a8ac-40e8-abc6-bb4e77e1dc87
  + [surface_uuid] is 0608e6ff-ecb3-4ded-86a5-3b8d59670410
  + [authority_scope] is post-FSC5 implementation chunk order, chunk readiness, gating rules, model routing, forbidden scope, expected outputs, and verification obligations
  + [implementation_scope] is implementation-readiness planning authority only
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC3_Runtime_Graph_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/planning/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop as the current post-FSC5 readiness surface
  = must: mint implementation slices before writing runtime code
  = must: preserve accepted SOP contract packs as boundary inputs
  = must: preserve that implementation planning does not authorize live operations control
  - never: treat post-FSC5 readiness records as machine-control permission

& [CanonicalImplementationReadinessChunkSet] is the post-FSC5 implementation chunk set
  + [chunk] is IR1 implementation substrate and repository scaffold
  + [chunk] is IR2 authority-file parser and SQLite projection builder
  + [chunk] is IR3 operator harness and fixture runner
  + [chunk] is IR4 LangGraph proof runtime implementation
  + [chunk] is IR5 surface projection prototype
  + [chunk] is IR6 coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype
  + [chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes the implementation surface
  = must: mark downstream chunks stale when an upstream accepted output changes

& [CanonicalImplementationReadinessModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR1] is requires deeper reasoning for repository shape, language/runtime choices, authority boundaries, and generated-artifact policy
  + [IR2] is requires deeper reasoning for parser correctness and projection authority boundaries; GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded parser fixtures after IR2 contracts are accepted
  + [IR3] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR1 and IR2 accepted if fixture runner scope is bounded by accepted contracts
  + [IR4] is requires deeper reasoning for LangGraph integration and interrupt semantics; GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded graph fixture implementation after proof contracts are accepted
  + [IR5] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable for bounded projection prototype after fixture records exist, with deeper reasoning for authority display conflicts
  + [IR6] is requires deeper reasoning for multi-agent coordination identity and conflict semantics
  + [IR7] is requires deeper reasoning for operations dry-run simulator boundaries; no live operations control authorized

  = must: state Spark suitability or deeper-reasoning requirement in every future work packet

